course: dictionary
lesson: 13172
title: Breaking into pieces
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fragmentation is a big word, but it has a simple core: something breaks into many small pieces. The word starts with «fragment», which means a small piece of something that has broken. «Roads and farms caused the fragmentation of the forest into small patches.» The clues are roads, farms and small patches, so fragmentation means the forest has been split into small, separate parts.
explain: The word can also describe a group, not just an object. «The fragmentation of the old empire led to many small states.» An empire is a large country ruled by one power. When it splits into many separate countries, that is fragmentation. The clue is the word «many»: one big thing has become lots of smaller things.
explain: Always check by swapping in a simpler idea. Try «breaking into small parts» in place of fragmentation. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found its meaning.
fact: Fragmentation means the breaking of something into small pieces.
fact: Fragmentation can also mean a group, country, habitat or system splitting into many smaller, separate parts.
fact: «Habitat fragmentation» happens when roads, farms and towns cut a forest into small patches, which can harm animals.
fact: «File fragmentation» is when a computer file is stored in scattered pieces, which can slow down an old hard drive.
fact: «The fragmentation of rock» can happen when rain and frost break a rock into smaller pieces over time.
exercise: «Roads and farms caused the fragmentation of the forest into small patches.» What does fragmentation mean here? | The forest growing much bigger | The forest catching fire | The forest being painted green | *The breaking of the forest into small, separate parts
exercise: «Old computers can slow down because of file fragmentation.» Which example shows file fragmentation? | A folder that is locked with a password | A bigger screen for watching films | A new keyboard with bright keys | *A file split into scattered pieces on an old hard drive
exercise: «The fragmentation of the old empire led to many small states.» What did the empire become? | *Many smaller, separate states | A forest full of trees | A single city with one king | One larger country
test: «Frost and rain caused the fragmentation of the rock, so the cliff crumbled.» What does fragmentation of the rock mean? | Melting the rock into water | *Breaking the rock into small pieces | Painting the rock a new colour | Making the rock bigger
test: Which example shows fragmentation of a group? | A pond that fills with rain | *A club that splits into several small groups | A bridge built from steel | A class that stays together on a trip
exam: Hannah says fragmentation means joining things together. Is she right? | Yes, it means making something very big | Yes, it means joining everything into one whole | *No, it means breaking into small, separate parts | No, it means the weather is wet
